From 3a1a0e6437c2455a7e0b93495e6a158d81524214 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chandler Newman <chandler2newman@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 20:22:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] vsock: deliver the resets queued for a restored device

A vsock device rebuilt from a snapshot queues a reset for every connection the
guest had open, because the host ends of those connections did not survive.
Nothing delivered them. The RX queue is processed when the guest posts buffers
or the backend has input, and a restored guest does neither: a peer blocked
reading a connection whose host end has gone sends nothing, and waits on it
forever.

Signal the RX queue once when the worker starts with resets pending. The
epoll loop does not run until the device is resumed, so the first pass after
resume delivers them and the guest sees ECONNRESET on each connection, which
is what lets it reconnect.
---
 virtio-devices/src/vsock/device.rs | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/virtio-devices/src/vsock/device.rs b/virtio-devices/src/vsock/device.rs
index 8cad82e72..2a5e4398a 100644
--- a/virtio-devices/src/vsock/device.rs
+++ b/virtio-devices/src/vsock/device.rs
@@ -217,6 +217,19 @@ fn run(
         helper.add_event(self.queue_evts[1].as_raw_fd(), TX_QUEUE_EVENT)?;
         helper.add_event(self.queue_evts[2].as_raw_fd(), EVT_QUEUE_EVENT)?;
         helper.add_event(self.backend.read().unwrap().get_polled_fd(), BACKEND_EVENT)?;
+
+        // A device rebuilt from a snapshot has queued a reset for every
+        // connection the guest had open, since the host ends of them did not
+        // survive. Nothing would deliver them: RX is processed when the guest
+        // posts buffers or the backend has input, and a restored guest does
+        // neither -- a peer blocked reading a dead connection sends nothing
+        // and waits forever. Signalling the RX queue once means the first
+        // pass of the loop, which runs only after the device is resumed,
+        // delivers them.
+        if self.backend.read().unwrap().has_pending_rx() {
+            self.queue_evts[0].write(1).map_err(EpollHelperError::IoError)?;
+        }
+
         helper.run(paused, paused_sync, self)?;
 
         Ok(())
